window.HADITH_DATA=window.HADITH_DATA.map(d=>d.id==="4563"?{"id":"4563","number":1,"title":"Islam, faith and ihsan","section":1,"sectionTitle":"Foundations of faith and Islam","slug":"01-islam-faith-and-ihsan","ref":"Sahih Muslim 8a","primary":"https://sunnah.com/muslim:8a","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","sourceUr":"https://hadeethenc.com/ur/browse/hadith/4563","ar":"عن عمر بن الخطاب رضي الله عنه قال: بَيْنَمَا نَحْنُ عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ذَاتَ يَوْمٍ إِذْ طَلَعَ عَلَيْنَا رَجُلٌ شَدِيدُ بَيَاضِ الثِّيَابِ، شَدِيدُ سَوَادِ الشَّعَرِ، لَا يُرَى عَلَيْهِ أَثَرُ السَّفَرِ، وَلَا يَعْرِفُهُ مِنَّا أَحَدٌ، حَتَّى جَلَسَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَسْنَدَ رُكْبَتَيْهِ إِلَى رُكْبَتَيْهِ، وَوَضَعَ كَفَّيْهِ عَلَى فَخِذَيْهِ، وَقَالَ: يَا مُحَمَّدُ، أَخْبِرْنِي عَنِ الْإِسْلَامِ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: «الْإِسْلَامُ أَنْ تَشْهَدَ أَنْ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللهُ، وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللهِ، وَتُقِيمَ الصَّلَاةَ، وَتُؤْتِيَ الزَّكَاةَ، وَتَصُومَ رَمَضَانَ، وَتَحُجَّ الْبَيْتَ إِنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ إِلَيْهِ سَبِيلًا» قَالَ: صَدَقْتَ، قَالَ: فَعَجِبْنَا لَهُ، يَسْأَلُهُ وَيُصَدِّقُهُ، قَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنِ الْإِيمَانِ، قَالَ: «أَنْ تُؤْمِنَ بِاللهِ، وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ، وَكُتُبِهِ، وَرُسُلِهِ، وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ، وَتُؤْمِنَ بِالْقَدَرِ خَيْرِهِ وَشَرِّهِ» قَالَ: صَدَقْتَ، قَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنِ الْإِحْسَانِ، قَالَ: «أَنْ تَعْبُدَ اللهَ كَأَنَّكَ تَرَاهُ، فَإِنْ لَمْ تَكُنْ تَرَاهُ فَإِنَّهُ يَرَاكَ» قَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنِ السَّاعَةِ، قَالَ: «مَا الْمَسْؤُولُ عَنْهَا بِأَعْلَمَ مِنَ السَّائِلِ» قَالَ: فَأَخْبِرْنِي عَنْ أَمَارَتِهَا، قَالَ: «أَنْ تَلِدَ الْأَمَةُ رَبَّتَهَا، وَأَنْ تَرَى الْحُفَاةَ الْعُرَاةَ الْعَالَةَ رِعَاءَ الشَّاءِ يَتَطَاوَلُونَ فِي الْبُنْيَانِ» قَالَ: ثُمَّ انْطَلَقَ، فَلَبِثْتُ مَلِيًّا ثُمَّ قَالَ لِي: «يَا عُمَرُ، أَتَدْرِي مَنِ السَّائِلُ؟» قُلْتُ: اللهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ، قَالَ: «فَإِنَّهُ جِبْرِيلُ، أَتَاكُمْ يُعَلِّمُكُمْ دِينَكُمْ».","en":"‘Umar ibn al-Khattāb (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: One day, we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) when there appeared before us a man dressed in extremely white clothes and had very black hair. No traces of travel were visible on him, and none of us knew him. He came in and sat down opposite the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him), rested his knees against his, and placed the palms of his hands on his (the Prophet's) thighs. He said: \"O Muhammad, tell me about Islam.\" The Messenger of Allah (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) said: \"Islam is to testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, to establish prayer, to pay Zakah, to fast Ramadan, and to perform Hajj to the House if you are able to find a way thereto.\" He said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" We wondered how he asked him and affirmed his truthfulness. Then, he said: \"Tell me about Imān (faith).\" He said: \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Last Day, and believe in the divine decree, the pleasant and unpleasant aspects thereof.\" Then, he said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then, he said: \"Tell me about ihsān.\" He said: \"It is to worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said: \"Tell me about the Hour.\" He said: \"The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.\" He said: \"Then, tell me about its signs.\" He said: \"The slave girl will give birth to her mistress, and you will see the barefoot, naked, and destitute herdsmen competing in constructing lofty buildings.\" Then, he departed. I stayed for a while, and then he said to me: \"O 'Umar, do you know who the questioner was?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"He was Jibrīl (Gabriel). He came to teach you your religion.\"","ur":"عمر بن خطاب رضی اللہ عنہ سے روایت ہے، وہ کہتے ہيں : ایک دن ہم رسول اللہ ﷺ کے پاس بیٹھے ہوئے تھے۔ اتنے میں ایک شخص آیا۔ اس کے کپڑے بہت سفید اور بال بہت کالے تھے۔ اس پر سفر کے آثار بھی نہیں دکھائی دے رہے تھے اور ہم میں سے کوئی اسے جانتا بھی نہیں تھا۔ وہ رسول اللہ ﷺ کے پاس آ کر بیٹھا۔ اپنے گھٹنے کو آپ کے گھٹنے سے لگا لیا اور اپنی ہتھیلیاں اپنى رانوں پر رکھی۔ پھر بولا : اے محمد (ﷺ)! مجھے اسلام کے بارے میں بتائیے؟ رسول اللہ ﷺ نے فرمایا : \"اسلام یہ ہے کہ تم اس بات کی گواہی دو کہ اللہ کے سوا کوئی عبادت کے لائق نہیں اور محمد (ﷺ) اس کے رسول ہیں، نماز قائم کرو، زکاۃ ادا کرو، رمضان کے روزے رکھو اور اگر اللہ کے گھر تک جانے کی استطاعت ہو، تو اس کا حج کرو۔\" یہ سن کر وہ بولا : آپ نے سچ فرمایا۔ ہمیں اس پر تعجب ہوا کہ وہ آپ سے سوال بھی کرتا ہے اور پھر خود آپ کی تصدیق بھی کرتا ہے۔ پھر بولا : مجھے ایمان کے بارے میں بتائیے۔ آپ ﷺ نے فرمایا : \"ایمان یہ ہے کہ تم اللہ پر، اس کے فرشتوں پر، اس کی کتابوں پر، اس کے رسولوں پر، آخرت کے دن پر اور ہر اچھی و بری تقدیر پر ایمان لاؤ\"۔ وہ بولا : آپ نے سچ فرمایا ۔ پھر بولا : مجھے احسان کے بارے میں بتائیے؟ آپ ﷺ نے فرمایا : \"اللہ کی عبادت اس طرح کرو، گویا تم اسے دیکھ رہے ہو اور اگر تم اسے نہیں دیکھ رہے ہو، تو وہ توتمھیں دیکھ رہا ہے\"۔ وہ کہنے لگا: اب مجھے قیامت کے بارے میں بتائیے؟ آپ ﷺ نے فرمایا : \"جس سے سوال کیا جا رہا ہے، وہ سوال کرنے والے سے زیادہ نہیں جانتا\"۔ اس نے کہا : اچھا تو مجھے اس کی نشانیاں بتائیے؟ آپ ﷺ نے فرمایا : \"(نشانیاں یہ ہیں کہ) لونڈی اپنی مالکن کو جنے گی۔ تم دیکھو گے کہ ننگے پاؤں، ننگے بدن، مفلس اور بکریاں چرانے والے لوگ محلات تعمیر کرنے میں ایک دوسرے پر فخر کیا کریں گے\"۔ اس کے بعد وہ چلا گیا۔ میں کچھ دیر تک ٹھہرا رہا۔ پھر آپ ﷺ نے فرمایا : \"اے عمر! کیا تم جانتے ہو کہ پوچھنے والا کون تھا؟\" میں نے عرض کیا : اللہ اور اس کا رسول زیادہ بہتر جانتے ہیں\"۔ آپ ﷺ نے فرمایا : \"وہ جبریل (علیہ السلام) تھے۔ وہ تمھیں تمھارے دین کے معاملات سکھانے آئے تھے\"۔","grade":"Authentic","gradeAr":"صحيح","attribution":"Narrated by Muslim","explanation":"'Umar ibn al-Khattāb (may Allah be pleased with him) informs that Jibrīl (peace be upon him) appeared before the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) in the form of an unknown man with white clothes and very dark hair and the signs of travel - such as fatigue, dust, unkempt hair, and dirty clothing - were not visible on him. None of those present knew him. This happened while they were sitting with the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him). He sat down before the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) as a learner and asked him about Islam. He answered him, pointing out the pillars of Islam: acknowledgment of the two testimonies of faith, observing the five prayers, paying the Zakah to its due recipients, fasting the month of Ramadan, and performing the obligation of Hajj for those who are able to do so.\r\n\r\nThe inquirer said: You have spoken the truth. The Companions wondered that he posed the question, which indicated that he apparently did not know the answer, and then he affirmed that the answer was right.\r\n\r\nThen, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation. Then, he asked him about ihsān, and the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) told him that ihsān is to worship Allah as if you can see Him, and if he cannot reach that level, he should then worship Allah Almighty as if Allah is watching him. The first is the level of watching, which is higher, and the second is the level of watchfulness.\r\n\r\nThen, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about the Hour, and he clarified that knowledge of the Hour is one of the things Allah kept to Himself alone; so, none of the creation knows it, neither the one inquired about it nor the inquirer.\r\n\r\nThen, he asked him about the signs of the Hour. He pointed out that its signs include the increasing number of slave girls or the prevalence of children's ingratitude toward their mothers as they treat them like slaves and that shepherds and poor people will lead a life of opulence in the latter times, taking pride in the construction and decoration of big houses.\r\n\r\nThen, the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) informed that the inquirer was Jibrīl, who came to teach the Companions this upright religion.","explanationUr":"عمر بن خطاب رضی اللہ عنہ بتا رہے ہیں کہ جبریل علیہ السلام صحابۂ کرام کے پاس ایک اجنبی شخص کی شکل اختیار کر کے آئے۔ ان کے کچھ صفات اس طرح تھے کہ ان کے کپڑے بہت زیادہ سفید اور بال بہت زیادہ کالے تھے۔ ان کے جسم پر سفر کا کوئی اثر، جیسے تھکاوٹ، دھول مٹی، بالوں کا بکھرا ہوا ہونا اور کپڑوں کا میلا کچیلا ہونا وغیرہ نہیں دکھ رہا تھا۔ وہاں موجود کوئی شخص ان کو پہچان بھی نہيں پا رہا تھا۔ اس وقت صحابہ اللہ کے رسول صلی اللہ علیہ و سلم کے پاس بیٹھے ہوئے تھے۔ وہ آپ کے سامنے ایک طالب علم کی طرح بیٹھ گئے اور اس کے بعد آپ سے اسلام کے بارے میں سوال کیا، تو آپ نے جو جواب دیا، اس میں دونوں گواہیوں کا اقرار، پانچ وقتوں کی نمازیں قائم کرنا، زکوۃ اس کے حق داروں کو دینا، رمضان مہینے کے روزے رکھنا اور استطاعت رکھنے والے کے لیے کعبہ کا حج کرنا شامل تھا۔\r\n\r\nجواب سننے کے بعد سوال کرنے والے نے کہا : آپ نے سچ کہا ہے۔ صحابہ کو اس بات کا تعجب ہوا ان کا سوال کرنا یہ دکھاتا ہے کہ وہ جانتے نہیں ہيں، لیکن وہ آپ کی بات کی تصدیق بھی کر رہے ہیں۔\r\n\r\nپھر انھوں نے آپ سے ایمان کے بارے میں پوچھا، تو آپ نے جو جواب دیا، اس میں ایمان کے چھ ارکان شامل ہيں، جو کچھ اس طرح ہيں؛ اللہ کے وجود اور اس کے صفات پر ایمان رکھنا، اسے اپنے افعال، جیسے تخلیق وغیرہ میں اکیلا ماننا اور بس اسی کو عبادت کا حق دار جاننا، اس بات پر ایمان رکھنا کہ فرشتے، جن کو اللہ نے نور سے پیدا کیا ہے، اس کے معزز بندے ہیں، جو اس کی نافرمانی نہيں کرتے اور اس کے ہر حکم کی تعمیل کرتے ہیں، اللہ کی جانب سے رسولوں پر اترنے والی کتابوں، جیسے قرآن، تورات اور انجیل وغیرہ پر ایمان رکھنا، انسانوں کو اللہ کا دین پہنچانے والے رسولوں، جیسے نوح، ابراہیم، موسی، عیسی اور آخری نبی محمد صلی اللہ علیہ و سلم پر ایمان رکھنا، آخرت کے دن پر ایمان رکھنا، جس میں موت کے بعد کی برزخی زندگی کے ساتھ ساتھ اس بات پر ایمان بھی شامل ہے کہ انسان کو موت کے بعد دوبارہ زندہ ہوکر اٹھنا اور حساب وکتاب کے مرحلہ سے گزرنا ہوگا، جس کے بعد اس کا ٹھکانہ یا تو جنت ہوگا یا پھر جہنم اور اخیر میں اس بات پر ایمان رکھنا کہ اللہ نے اپنے سابقہ علم اور اپنی حکمت کے مطابق ساری چیزوں کی مقدار مقرر کرکے ان کو لکھ رکھا ہے اور بعد میں وہ ساری چیزیں اللہ کے ارادے سے اور اس کے اندازے کے مطابق ہی سامنے آتی ہيں اور وہی ان کی تخلیق بھی کرتا ہے۔ پھر انھوں نے آپ سے احسان کے بارے میں پوچھا، تو آپ نے بتایا کہ احسان یہ ہے کہ انسان اللہ کی عبادت اس طرح کرے، گویا وہ اللہ کو دیکھ رہا ہے۔ اگر وہ اس مقام تک نہ پہنچ سکے، تو اللہ کی عبادت یہ سوچ کر کرے کہ اللہ اسے دیکھ رہا ہے۔ یہاں پہلا مقام مشاہدے کا ہے، جو کہ سب سے اونچا ہے اور دوسرا مقام مراقبے کا ہے۔\r\n\r\nپھر انھوں نے آپ سے پوچھا کہ قیامت کب آئے گی، تو اللہ کے نبی صلی اللہ علیہ و سلم  نے بتایا کہ قیامت کب آئے گی، یہ بات ان باتوں میں سے ہے، جن کو اللہ نے کسی کو نہيں بتایا ہے۔ لہذا اس کا علم کسی کے پاس نہيں ہے۔ نہ جس سے پوچھا گیا ہے، اس کے پاس اور نہ پوچھنے والے کے پاس۔\r\n\r\nبعد ازاں انھوں نے آپ سے قیامت کی نشانیوں کے بارے میں پوچھا، تو آپ نے بتایا کہ اس کی ایک نشانی یہ ہے کہ باندیوں اور اس کے بطن سے جنم لینے والے بچوں کی بہتات ہوگی یا پھر یہ کہ بچے اپنی ماؤں کی بہت زیادہ نافرمانی کرنے لگیں گے اور ان کے ساتھ باندیوں جیسا سلوک کریں گے۔ دوسری نشانی یہ ہے کہ آخری زمانے میں بکریوں کے چرواہوں اور فقیروں کے سامنے دنیا کے دروازے کھول دیے جائیں گے اور وہ خوب صورت اور مضبوط محلوں کے معاملے میں ایک دوسرے پر فخر کریں گے۔\r\n\r\nاخیر میں اللہ کے نبی صلی اللہ علیہ و سلم نے بتایا کہ پوچھنے والے جبریل تھے، جو صحابہ کو اسلام سکھانے کے لیے آئے تھے۔","hints":["The Hadīth shows the Prophet’s good manners and that he would sit with his Companions, and they would attend to him.\r","A questioner should be treated in a gentle and friendly manner so that he can pose the question without reservation or fear.\r","A teacher should be treated in a polite manner, as Jibrīl (peace be upon him) sat down before the Prophet (may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him) in a polite way to learn from him.\r","The pillars of Islam are five and the fundamentals of faith are six.\r","When Islam and faith are mentioned together, Islam is taken to refer to the outward aspects, whereas faith is taken to refer to the inward ones.\r","Religion has varying levels. The first level is Islam, the second is Imān (faith), and the third is ihsān, which is the highest one.\r","A questioner typically lacks knowledge, and it is his ignorance that drives him to ask. Therefore, the Companions wondered that he posed the question and affirmed the soundness of the answer.\r","First things first. He began with the two testimonies of faith when defining Islam and began with belief in Allah when defining faith.\r","A scholar may be asked about something the questioner already knows so that others can learn it.\r","Knowledge about the Hour is part of the knowledge Allah kept to Himself alone."],"hintsUr":["اللہ کے نبی صلی اللہ علیہ و سلم کا اعلی اخلاق کہ آپ اپنے ساتھیوں کے ساتھ گھل مل کر بیٹھ جایا کرتے تھے۔\r","سوال کرنے والے کے ساتھ نرمی بھرا برتاؤ کرنا اور اسے اپنے پاس بٹھانا چاہیے، تاکہ وہ بغیر کسی خوف اور تردد کے جو کچھ پوچھنا چاہے، پوچھ سکے۔\r","استاد کے ساتھ ادب و احترام کا معاملہ کرنا چاہیے۔ ہم یہاں دیکھتے ہیں کہ جبریل علیہ السلام اللہ کے نبی صلی اللہ علیہ و سلم کے سامنے ادب کے ساتھ بیٹھ گئے، تاکہ آپ سے علم حاصل کر سکیں۔\r","اسلام کے پانچ ارکان اور ایمان کی چھ بنیادیں ہيں۔\r","جب اسلام اور ایمان دونوں الفاظ ایک ساتھ آئیں، تو اسلام کی تفسیر ظاہری چیزوں سے کی جائے گی اور ایمان کی تفسیر باطنی چیزوں سے۔\r","دین کے مختلف درجات ہيں۔ پہلا درجہ اسلام ہے، دوسرا ایمان ہے اور تیسرا احسان، جو کہ دین کا سب سے اونچا درجہ ہے۔\r","اصل یہ ہے کہ پوچھنے والے کے پاس جانکاری نہ ہو اور عدم واقفیت کی وجہ سے ہی انسان کسی سے کچھ پوچھتا ہے۔ یہی وجہ ہے کہ صحابہ کو اس بات پر تعجب ہوا کہ وہ شخص خود پوچھ بھی رہا تھا اور تصدیق بھی کر رہا تھا۔\r","آغاز زیادہ اہم سے کر کے کم اہم کی طرف جانا چاہیے۔ یہی وجہ ہے کہ اسلام کی تفسیر کرتے وقت آغاز دونوں گواہیوں سے کیا گيا اور ایمان کی تفسیر کرتے وقت آغاز اللہ پر ایمان سے کیا گیا۔\r","دین کا علم رکھنے والوں سے ایسی چیزوں کے بارے میں پوچھا جا سکتا ہے، جن سے پوچھنے والا واقف ہو، تاکہ دوسرے لوگ بھی ان چیزوں کو جان جائیں۔\r","قیامت کب آئے گی، اس بات کا علم اللہ نے اپنے پاس رکھا ہے۔"],"explanationAr":"يُخبِرُ عمر بن الخطاب رضي الله عنه أنّ جبريل عليه السلام خرج على الصحابة رضي الله عنهم بصورةِ رجلٍ لا يُعرف، ومن صفاته أنّ ثيابَه شديدة البياض، وشعرَه شديد السواد، لا يُرى عليه أَثَرُ السَّفَر من ظهور التعب، والغبار، وتفرُّق الشَّعَر، واتساخ الثياب، ولا يَعرفه أحدٌ من الحاضرين، وهم جلوس عند النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، فَجَلسَ بين يدي النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم جِلْسَة المُتَعلِّم، فسأله عن الإسلام، فأجابه بهذه الأركان التي تتضمن الإقرار بالشهادتين، والمحافظة على الصلوات الخمس، وأداء الزكاة لمستحقيها، وصيام شهر رمضان، وأداء فريضة الحج على المستطيع.\n\nفقال السائل: صدقت، فاستغرب الصحابةُ من سؤالِه الدَّالِّ على عَدَمِ معرفتِه فيما يَظهر ثم تصديقِه.\n\nثم سأله عن الإيمان، فأجابه بهذه الأركان الستة المتضمنة الإيمان بوجود الله تعالى وصفاته، وإفراده بأفعاله كالخلق، وإفراده بالعبادة، وأن الملائكة التي خلقها الله من نور عباد مُكْرَمون لا يعصون الله تعالى وبأمره يعملون، والإيمان بالكتب المنزلة على الرُّسُل من عند الله تعالى، كالقرآن والتوراة والإنجيل وغيرها، وبالرسل المبلِّغين عن الله دينَه، ومنهم نوح وإبراهيم وموسى وعيسى وآخرهم محمد صلى الله عليهم وسلم، وغيرهم من الأنبياء والرسل، والإيمان باليوم الآخر، ويدخل فيه ما بعد الموت من القبر والحياة البرزخية، وأن الإنسان يُبعث بعد الموت ويُحاسب، ويكون مصيره إما إلى الجنة أو النار، والإيمان بأنَّ الله قدَّرَ الأشياء حسبما سَبَق به علمُه واقتضته حكمتُه وكتابته لذلك، ومشيئته له، ووقوعها على حسب ما قدَّرها، وخلقَه لها.\n \nثم سأله عن الإحسان، فأخبره أن الإحسان أن يَعبُدَ اللهَ كأنه يراه، فإن لم يَتَحقَّق له الوصولُ إلى هذه المنزلة فلْيَعبُدِ اللهَ تعالى كأنَّ اللهَ يُشاهدُه، فالأولى منزلة المشاهدة، وهي أعلى، والثانية منزلة المراقبة.\n\nثم سأله متى الساعة؟ فبيَّن النبيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم أنَّ عِلْمَ الساعة ممّا استأثر الله بعلمه، فلا يعلمه أحد من الخلق، لا المسؤول عنها ولا السائل.\n\nثم سأله عن علامات الساعة؟ فبين أنَّ مِن علاماتِها كثرةَ السراري وأولادِها، أو كثرةَ عقوقِ الأولاد لأمهاتِهم يعاملونهن معاملة الإماء، وأن رعاةَ الغنم والفقراء تُبسط لهم الدنيا في آخر الزمان، فيتفاخرون في زخرفة المباني وتشييدِها.\n\nثم أخبر النبيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم أنَّ السائل هو جبريل جاء لتعليم الصحابة هذا الدين الحنيف.","hintsAr":["حُسْن خُلُقِ النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، وأنه يجلس مع أصحابه ويجلسون إليه.","مشروعية الرفق بالسائل وتقريبه، ليتمكن من السؤال غير مُنْقَبِضٍ ولا خائف.","الأدب مع المعلِّم كما فعل جبريل عليه السلام، حيث جلس أمام النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم جِلْسَة المتأدِّب ليأخذ منه.","أركان الإسلام خمسة، وأصولَ الإيمان ستة.","عند اجتماع الإسلام والإيمان يُفسَّر الإسلام بالأمور الظاهرة، والإيمان بالأمور الباطنة.","بيان أن الدين درجات متفاوتة، فالدرجة الأولى :الإسلام، والثانية :الإيمان، والثالثة: الإحسان، وهو أعلاها.","الأصل في السائل عدم العلم، والجهل هو الباعث على السؤال، لذلك عَجِب الصحابةُ من سؤالِه وتصديقِه.","البدء بالأهمِّ فالأهمِّ؛ لأنَّه بُدىء بالشهادَتين في تفسير الإسلام، وبُدىء بالإيمان بالله في تفسير الإيمان.","سؤال أهل العلم ما لا يجهله السائل، ليعلم غيره.","علم الساعة مِمَّا استأثر الله بعلمه."],"words":[],"publisher":"HadeethEnc.com","retrieved":"2026-10-17","narrator":"Umar ibn al-Khattab"}:d);window.LEARNING_DATA={"4563":{"revision":"topic002-coverage-2026-10-17","narrator":"Umar ibn al-Khattab","qa":[{"id":"4563-qa-1","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"How are Islam, iman and ihsan distinguished in Jibril's questions?","a":"In this account, Islam is explained through the outward pillars, iman through six foundations of belief, and ihsan through worship with awareness of Allah. The benefits qualify the distinction between Islam and iman when the two are mentioned together. These are connected dimensions of religion, not independent paths that replace one another.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published benefit 5","text":"When Islam and faith are mentioned together, Islam is taken to refer to the outward aspects, whereas faith is taken to refer to the inward ones.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"mentioned together","field":"B5"}},{"id":"4563-qa-2","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"What are the six foundations of belief named in the report?","a":"They are belief in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Last Day, and divine decree in its pleasant and unpleasant aspects. The list connects faith with revelation, accountability, and Allah's knowledge and decree. The explanation develops each foundation; it does not reduce faith to outward identification alone.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"Then, he said: \"Tell me about Imān (faith).\" He said: \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Last Day, and believe in the divine decree, the pleasant and unpleasant aspects thereof.\" Then, he said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then, he said: \"Tell me about ihsān.\" He said: \"It is to worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said: \"Tell me about the Hour.\" He said: \"The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.\" He said: \"Then, tell me about its signs.\" He said: \"The slave girl will give birth to her mistress, and you will see the barefoot, naked, and destitute herdsmen competing in constructing lofty buildings.\" Then, he departed.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"His angels, His books","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-qa-3","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"What does ihsan add to the practice of worship?","a":"The Prophet describes worshipping Allah as if one sees Him, and knowing that He sees the worshipper even when the worshipper does not see Him. The focus is attentive awareness of Allah while worshipping. The account also distinguishes knowing the signs of the Hour from knowing its time, which is not given to the questioner or respondent.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"Then, he said: \"Tell me about Imān (faith).\" He said: \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Last Day, and believe in the divine decree, the pleasant and unpleasant aspects thereof.\" Then, he said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then, he said: \"Tell me about ihsān.\" He said: \"It is to worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said: \"Tell me about the Hour.\" He said: \"The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.\" He said: \"Then, tell me about its signs.\" He said: \"The slave girl will give birth to her mistress, and you will see the barefoot, naked, and destitute herdsmen competing in constructing lofty buildings.\" Then, he departed.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"He sees you","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-qa-4","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"Which five outward foundations does the Prophet name when asked about Islam?","a":"He names the two testimonies, establishing prayer, paying zakat, fasting Ramadan and pilgrimage to the House when one is able. The condition of ability is expressly attached to Hajj in this account; the list should be taught with that condition retained.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"He said: \"O Muhammad, tell me about Islam.\" The Messenger of Allah (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) said: \"Islam is to testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, to establish prayer, to pay Zakah, to fast Ramadan, and to perform Hajj to the House if you are able to find a way thereto.\" He said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" We wondered how he asked him and affirmed his truthfulness.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"if you are able","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-qa-5","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"What does belief in Allah include in the explanation of iman?","a":"It includes belief in His existence and attributes, recognizing His actions such as creation as His alone, and devoting worship exclusively to Him. The explanation joins acknowledgment of Allah with His sole right to worship.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"devoting worship","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-qa-6","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"How does the explanation describe belief in angels and revealed Books?","a":"It describes angels as honored servants who obey Allah, and the Books as scriptures He revealed to His messengers. These beliefs recognize both the messengers of revelation and its divine origin, rather than reducing faith to what human beings can directly observe.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"honorable servants","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-qa-7","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"How does the explanation describe belief in the messengers?","a":"They conveyed Allah's religion. The explanation names Noah, Abraham, Moses and Jesus among them, and Muhammad as the last. Belief therefore includes the messengers Allah sent, not accepting the final message while rejecting earlier prophets.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"messengers who conveyed","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-qa-8","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"What does belief in the Last Day include in the published explanation?","a":"It includes life after death, resurrection, reckoning and the final outcome in Paradise or Hellfire. The explanation therefore gives accountability a place within the foundations of belief, not merely a vague expectation that history will end.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"reckoning","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-qa-9","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"How is belief in decree explained beyond accepting only pleasant events?","a":"The report includes its pleasant and unpleasant aspects. The explanation connects all that occurs with Allah's prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, will and creation. The definition does not limit decree to outcomes a person prefers.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"prior knowledge","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-qa-10","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"Why does the answer about the Hour not give its date?","a":"The Prophet says the one questioned knows no more than the questioner. The explanation identifies the time of the Hour as knowledge Allah has kept to Himself. Knowing signs is therefore distinct from possessing its exact date.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"Then, he said: \"Tell me about Imān (faith).\" He said: \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Last Day, and believe in the divine decree, the pleasant and unpleasant aspects thereof.\" Then, he said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then, he said: \"Tell me about ihsān.\" He said: \"It is to worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said: \"Tell me about the Hour.\" He said: \"The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.\" He said: \"Then, tell me about its signs.\" He said: \"The slave girl will give birth to her mistress, and you will see the barefoot, naked, and destitute herdsmen competing in constructing lofty buildings.\" Then, he departed.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"knows no more","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-qa-11","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"Which two signs are mentioned, and how does the source discuss them?","a":"The report mentions a slave girl giving birth to her mistress and destitute herdsmen competing in lofty buildings. The explanation discusses the first through changes involving slave girls or children's ingratitude toward mothers, and the second through former poverty changing into display and competition. These are the source's explanations, not a timetable naming particular people or countries.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"He pointed out that its signs include the increasing number of slave girls or the prevalence of children's ingratitude toward their mothers as they treat them like slaves and that shepherds and poor people will lead a life of opulence in the latter times, taking pride in the construction and decoration of big houses.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"ingratitude","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-qa-12","group":"Meaning and understanding","q":"How did Jibril's questions teach people other than the questioner?","a":"He asked and then confirmed the answers, which surprised the companions. At the end the Prophet identified him and explained that he had come to teach their religion. The benefits explicitly recognize asking a scholar a question one already knows so that others can learn.","origin":"Editorial explanation based on the linked publisher material","lang":"en","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published benefit 9","text":"A scholar may be asked about something the questioner already knows so that others can learn it.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"others can learn","field":"B9"}}],"mcq":[{"id":"4563-mc-1","q":"Which distinction follows the definitions when Islam and iman are mentioned together here?","options":["Islam describes outward pillars; iman describes foundations of belief","Islam describes voluntary deeds; iman describes only obligatory deeds","Islam concerns belief in angels; iman concerns only pilgrimage","Islam and iman designate two unrelated religious paths"],"correct":0,"feedback":["The source distinguishes outward observance and inward belief when the terms occur together, while presenting both within the religion.","The supported answer is: Islam describes outward pillars; iman describes foundations of belief. The source distinguishes outward observance and inward belief when the terms occur together, while presenting both within the religion.","The supported answer is: Islam describes outward pillars; iman describes foundations of belief. The source distinguishes outward observance and inward belief when the terms occur together, while presenting both within the religion.","The supported answer is: Islam describes outward pillars; iman describes foundations of belief. The source distinguishes outward observance and inward belief when the terms occur together, while presenting both within the religion."],"hint":"Compare the two answers before the question about ihsan.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published benefit 5","text":"When Islam and faith are mentioned together, Islam is taken to refer to the outward aspects, whereas faith is taken to refer to the inward ones.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"mentioned together","field":"B5"}},{"id":"4563-mc-2","q":"A worshipper remembers that Allah sees them even when no person is present. Which teaching does this apply?","options":["Knowledge of the exact time of the Hour","Ihsan as attentive awareness of Allah","The numerical order of the five pillars","The distinction between zakat recipients"],"correct":1,"feedback":["The supported answer is: Ihsan as attentive awareness of Allah. The definition of ihsan directly connects worship with awareness that Allah sees the worshipper.","The definition of ihsan directly connects worship with awareness that Allah sees the worshipper.","The supported answer is: Ihsan as attentive awareness of Allah. The definition of ihsan directly connects worship with awareness that Allah sees the worshipper.","The supported answer is: Ihsan as attentive awareness of Allah. The definition of ihsan directly connects worship with awareness that Allah sees the worshipper."],"hint":"Consider the description of worship after the questions about Islam and iman.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"Then, he said: \"Tell me about Imān (faith).\" He said: \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Last Day, and believe in the divine decree, the pleasant and unpleasant aspects thereof.\" Then, he said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then, he said: \"Tell me about ihsān.\" He said: \"It is to worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said: \"Tell me about the Hour.\" He said: \"The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.\" He said: \"Then, tell me about its signs.\" He said: \"The slave girl will give birth to her mistress, and you will see the barefoot, naked, and destitute herdsmen competing in constructing lofty buildings.\" Then, he departed.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"He sees you","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-mc-3","q":"Which pilgrimage condition is retained in the definition of Islam here?","options":["A journey required regardless of all ability","Ability to find a way to the House","Residence in Makkah before accepting Islam","Prior knowledge of the exact time of the Hour"],"correct":1,"feedback":["The supported answer is: Ability to find a way to the House. The report expressly qualifies Hajj by ability.","The report expressly qualifies Hajj by ability.","The supported answer is: Ability to find a way to the House. The report expressly qualifies Hajj by ability.","The supported answer is: Ability to find a way to the House. The report expressly qualifies Hajj by ability."],"hint":"Read the final qualification in the answer about Islam.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"He said: \"O Muhammad, tell me about Islam.\" The Messenger of Allah (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) said: \"Islam is to testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, to establish prayer, to pay Zakah, to fast Ramadan, and to perform Hajj to the House if you are able to find a way thereto.\" He said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" We wondered how he asked him and affirmed his truthfulness.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"if you are able","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-mc-4","q":"Which set correctly completes belief in Allah, angels, Books and messengers?","options":["Worldly success and uninterrupted comfort","The Last Day and decree in its pleasant and unpleasant aspects","Family standing and public recognition","The exact date of the Hour and the identity of every future ruler"],"correct":1,"feedback":["The supported answer is: The Last Day and decree in its pleasant and unpleasant aspects. The answer lists six foundations, including accountability and decree.","The answer lists six foundations, including accountability and decree.","The supported answer is: The Last Day and decree in its pleasant and unpleasant aspects. The answer lists six foundations, including accountability and decree.","The supported answer is: The Last Day and decree in its pleasant and unpleasant aspects. The answer lists six foundations, including accountability and decree."],"hint":"Keep the last two foundations distinct from knowledge not granted in the account.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"Then, he said: \"Tell me about Imān (faith).\" He said: \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Last Day, and believe in the divine decree, the pleasant and unpleasant aspects thereof.\" Then, he said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then, he said: \"Tell me about ihsān.\" He said: \"It is to worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said: \"Tell me about the Hour.\" He said: \"The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.\" He said: \"Then, tell me about its signs.\" He said: \"The slave girl will give birth to her mistress, and you will see the barefoot, naked, and destitute herdsmen competing in constructing lofty buildings.\" Then, he departed.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"pleasant and unpleasant","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-mc-5","q":"Which account of belief in Allah matches the explanation?","options":["Recognizing His existence while sharing worship with another","Treating creation as outside His power","Affirming Him, His attributes and exclusive worship","Making public recognition the basis of His right to worship"],"correct":2,"feedback":["The supported answer is: Affirming Him, His attributes and exclusive worship. The explanation brings together existence, attributes, divine actions and exclusive devotion.","The supported answer is: Affirming Him, His attributes and exclusive worship. The explanation brings together existence, attributes, divine actions and exclusive devotion.","The explanation brings together existence, attributes, divine actions and exclusive devotion.","The supported answer is: Affirming Him, His attributes and exclusive worship. The explanation brings together existence, attributes, divine actions and exclusive devotion."],"hint":"Read all parts of the first foundation's explanation.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"devoting worship","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-mc-6","q":"How are angels described in the published explanation?","options":["Honored servants who obey Allah's commands","Independent beings who share Allah's right to worship","Human scholars whose opinions replace revelation","Created beings free to overturn every divine command"],"correct":0,"feedback":["The explanation affirms their created servanthood and obedience.","The supported answer is: Honored servants who obey Allah's commands. The explanation affirms their created servanthood and obedience.","The supported answer is: Honored servants who obey Allah's commands. The explanation affirms their created servanthood and obedience.","The supported answer is: Honored servants who obey Allah's commands. The explanation affirms their created servanthood and obedience."],"hint":"Read the description given when the foundations of faith are expanded.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"honorable servants","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-mc-7","q":"What does belief in the revealed Books affirm in the explanation?","options":["That every later human statement has the status of revelation","That Allah sent scriptures to His messengers","That revealed guidance has no role in faith","That acknowledging one messenger requires denying every earlier revelation"],"correct":1,"feedback":["The supported answer is: That Allah sent scriptures to His messengers. The explanation names scriptures revealed by Allah, including the Quran, Torah and Gospel.","The explanation names scriptures revealed by Allah, including the Quran, Torah and Gospel.","The supported answer is: That Allah sent scriptures to His messengers. The explanation names scriptures revealed by Allah, including the Quran, Torah and Gospel.","The supported answer is: That Allah sent scriptures to His messengers. The explanation names scriptures revealed by Allah, including the Quran, Torah and Gospel."],"hint":"Distinguish divine revelation from claims made without it.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"scriptures revealed","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-mc-8","q":"How are the messengers described in the explanation?","options":["Replacing divine revelation with competing personal religions","Being independent objects of worship alongside Allah","Conveying Allah's religion, with Muhammad the last of them","Removing the need to believe in any earlier messenger"],"correct":2,"feedback":["The supported answer is: Conveying Allah's religion, with Muhammad the last of them. The explanation gives their shared role and names the final messenger.","The supported answer is: Conveying Allah's religion, with Muhammad the last of them. The explanation gives their shared role and names the final messenger.","The explanation gives their shared role and names the final messenger.","The supported answer is: Conveying Allah's religion, with Muhammad the last of them. The explanation gives their shared role and names the final messenger."],"hint":"Keep their mission distinct from Allah's exclusive right to worship.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"messengers who conveyed","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-mc-9","q":"Which sequence belongs to belief in the Last Day as explained here?","options":["Worldly wealth, public office and immunity from accountability","The date of the Hour being known by every messenger","Life after death, resurrection, reckoning and final recompense","Human beings deciding their final fate independently of Allah"],"correct":2,"feedback":["The supported answer is: Life after death, resurrection, reckoning and final recompense. The explanation expands the Last Day through the realities of accountability.","The supported answer is: Life after death, resurrection, reckoning and final recompense. The explanation expands the Last Day through the realities of accountability.","The explanation expands the Last Day through the realities of accountability.","The supported answer is: Life after death, resurrection, reckoning and final recompense. The explanation expands the Last Day through the realities of accountability."],"hint":"Read beyond the short name of the foundation.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"reckoning","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-mc-10","q":"Which belief about decree matches the explanation?","options":["Events occur according to Allah's prior knowledge, wisdom, writing and will","Only events people enjoy belong to divine decree","An unpleasant outcome proves there was no divine knowledge of it","Decree removes the need for every act of obedience"],"correct":0,"feedback":["The definition includes pleasant and unpleasant aspects, and the explanation gives its foundations.","The supported answer is: Events occur according to Allah's prior knowledge, wisdom, writing and will. The definition includes pleasant and unpleasant aspects, and the explanation gives its foundations.","The supported answer is: Events occur according to Allah's prior knowledge, wisdom, writing and will. The definition includes pleasant and unpleasant aspects, and the explanation gives its foundations.","The supported answer is: Events occur according to Allah's prior knowledge, wisdom, writing and will. The definition includes pleasant and unpleasant aspects, and the explanation gives its foundations."],"hint":"Keep personal preference distinct from the scope of decree.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published explanation","text":"Then, he asked the Prophet (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) about faith, and he answered him listing the six pillars that contain belief in the existence of Allah Almighty and His attributes, ascribing His actions, such as creation, to Him alone, and devoting worship only to Him; belief that the angels, whom Allah created from light, are honorable servants who do not disobey Allah Almighty and they execute His commands; belief in the scriptures revealed by Allah Almighty to the messengers, like the Qur’an, the Torah, and the Gospel, and in the messengers who conveyed Allah's religion, such as Noah, Abraham, Moses, Jesus, and the last of them Muhammad (peace be upon all of them); belief in the Last Day, which includes the barzakh life (life after death in the grave) and that every human being will be resurrected after death and undergo the reckoning and will ultimately end up in Paradise or Hellfire; and belief that Allah had predestined all things according to His prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, and will, and that everything happens according to Allah's predestination and creation.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"prior knowledge","field":"E"}},{"id":"4563-mc-11","q":"What is the distinction between the Hour and its signs in the exchange?","options":["The signs supply an exact calendar date","Both questioner and respondent claim to know its date","Its time is not disclosed, while certain signs are described","Discussing signs cancels belief in final accountability"],"correct":2,"feedback":["The supported answer is: Its time is not disclosed, while certain signs are described. The answer denies knowledge of the time shared by the questioner or respondent, then states signs.","The supported answer is: Its time is not disclosed, while certain signs are described. The answer denies knowledge of the time shared by the questioner or respondent, then states signs.","The answer denies knowledge of the time shared by the questioner or respondent, then states signs.","The supported answer is: Its time is not disclosed, while certain signs are described. The answer denies knowledge of the time shared by the questioner or respondent, then states signs."],"hint":"Follow the order from the question about time to the question about signs.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"Then, he said: \"Tell me about Imān (faith).\" He said: \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Last Day, and believe in the divine decree, the pleasant and unpleasant aspects thereof.\" Then, he said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then, he said: \"Tell me about ihsān.\" He said: \"It is to worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said: \"Tell me about the Hour.\" He said: \"The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.\" He said: \"Then, tell me about its signs.\" He said: \"The slave girl will give birth to her mistress, and you will see the barefoot, naked, and destitute herdsmen competing in constructing lofty buildings.\" Then, he departed.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"knows no more","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-mc-12","q":"Which pair of signs is actually mentioned in this selection?","options":["The rising of a named ruler and a specified calendar year","A slave girl giving birth to her mistress and poor herdsmen competing in lofty buildings","The companions leaving Madinah and the end of every building project","A prohibition of all construction and the disappearance of every flock"],"correct":1,"feedback":["The supported answer is: A slave girl giving birth to her mistress and poor herdsmen competing in lofty buildings. These are the two signs in the selected wording; it supplies no named contemporary country or date.","These are the two signs in the selected wording; it supplies no named contemporary country or date.","The supported answer is: A slave girl giving birth to her mistress and poor herdsmen competing in lofty buildings. These are the two signs in the selected wording; it supplies no named contemporary country or date.","The supported answer is: A slave girl giving birth to her mistress and poor herdsmen competing in lofty buildings. These are the two signs in the selected wording; it supplies no named contemporary country or date."],"hint":"Use the narrated wording rather than an added prediction.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"Then, he said: \"Tell me about Imān (faith).\" He said: \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, and the Last Day, and believe in the divine decree, the pleasant and unpleasant aspects thereof.\" Then, he said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then, he said: \"Tell me about ihsān.\" He said: \"It is to worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said: \"Tell me about the Hour.\" He said: \"The one questioned about it knows no more than the questioner.\" He said: \"Then, tell me about its signs.\" He said: \"The slave girl will give birth to her mistress, and you will see the barefoot, naked, and destitute herdsmen competing in constructing lofty buildings.\" Then, he departed.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"lofty buildings","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-mc-13","q":"Why was the visitor's confirmation of the answers surprising to the companions?","options":["He denied every answer after requesting it","He demanded that the companions answer instead of the Prophet","He asked as a learner and then affirmed the answers' truth","He refused to speak until his identity was announced"],"correct":2,"feedback":["The supported answer is: He asked as a learner and then affirmed the answers' truth. The report and explanation identify this combination as the source of their wonder.","The supported answer is: He asked as a learner and then affirmed the answers' truth. The report and explanation identify this combination as the source of their wonder.","The report and explanation identify this combination as the source of their wonder.","The supported answer is: He asked as a learner and then affirmed the answers' truth. The report and explanation identify this combination as the source of their wonder."],"hint":"Notice what happens after each answer.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published English selection","text":"He said: \"O Muhammad, tell me about Islam.\" The Messenger of Allah (may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him) said: \"Islam is to testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, to establish prayer, to pay Zakah, to fast Ramadan, and to perform Hajj to the House if you are able to find a way thereto.\" He said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" We wondered how he asked him and affirmed his truthfulness.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"We wondered","field":"T"}},{"id":"4563-mc-14","q":"What teaching purpose is revealed when the visitor's identity is explained?","options":["A knowledgeable questioner can ask so that others learn","Only someone ignorant may ever ask a scholar a question","The visitor came to supply a new religion after the Prophet's answer","The questions were intended to replace worship with argument"],"correct":0,"feedback":["The closing explanation identifies Jibril's teaching purpose and the benefits recognize this method.","The supported answer is: A knowledgeable questioner can ask so that others learn. The closing explanation identifies Jibril's teaching purpose and the benefits recognize this method.","The supported answer is: A knowledgeable questioner can ask so that others learn. The closing explanation identifies Jibril's teaching purpose and the benefits recognize this method.","The supported answer is: A knowledgeable questioner can ask so that others learn. The closing explanation identifies Jibril's teaching purpose and the benefits recognize this method."],"hint":"Read the final identification together with the teaching benefit.","category":"Content practice","source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","evidence":{"label":"Published benefit 9","text":"A scholar may be asked about something the questioner already knows so that others can learn it.","url":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","anchor":"others can learn","field":"B9"}}],"source":"https://hadeethenc.com/en/browse/hadith/4563","coverage":{"focusedAnswers":12,"thematicQuestions":14,"completeSanadProvided":false,"topics":[{"point":"Islam, iman and ihsan as connected levels, with the paired-term qualification","qa":[1],"mcq":[1]},{"point":"Five pillars and the explicit condition of ability for Hajj","qa":[4],"mcq":[3]},{"point":"Six foundations of belief, including decree's pleasant and unpleasant aspects","qa":[2],"mcq":[4]},{"point":"Belief in Allah: existence, attributes, divine actions and exclusive worship","qa":[5],"mcq":[5]},{"point":"Angels as obedient created servants and Books as divine revelation","qa":[6],"mcq":[6,7]},{"point":"Messengers conveying Allah's religion and Muhammad as the last messenger","qa":[7],"mcq":[8]},{"point":"The Last Day: life after death, resurrection, reckoning and recompense","qa":[8],"mcq":[9]},{"point":"Decree in Allah's prior knowledge, wisdom, writing, will and creation","qa":[9],"mcq":[10]},{"point":"Ihsan and awareness that Allah sees the worshipper","qa":[3],"mcq":[2]},{"point":"The time of the Hour distinguished from its signs","qa":[10],"mcq":[11]},{"point":"The two stated signs and the publisher's explanations without a timetable","qa":[11],"mcq":[12]},{"point":"Jibril's identity, the companions' surprise and learning through questions","qa":[12],"mcq":[13,14]}]}}};